cle, and set up the vail of the covering, and covered the ark of the testimony; as the LORD commanded Moses.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter(«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrAnd he put the table in the tent of the congregation, upon the side of the tabernacle northward, without the vail.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWAnd he set the bread in order upon it before the LORD; as the LORD had commanded Moses.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|And he put the candlestick in the tent of the congregation, over against the table, on the side of the tabernacle southward.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFAnd he lighted the lamps before the LORD; as the LORD commanded Moses.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙLAnd he put the golden altar in the tent of the congregation before the vail:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ@and he burnt sweet incense thereon; as the LORD commanded Moses.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ8And he set up the hanging at the door of the tabernacle.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter(«first_verseªlast_verse!¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÀAnd he put the altar of burnt offering by the door of the tabernacle of the tent of the congregation, and offered upon it the burnt offering and the meat offering; as the LORD commanded Moses.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmAnd he set the laver between the tent of the congregation and the altar, and put water there, to wash withal.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKAnd Moses and Aaron and his sons washed their hands and their feet thereat:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒwhen they went into the tent of the congregation, and when they came near unto the altar, they washed; as the LORD commanded Moses.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŠAnd he reared up the court round about the tabernacle and the altar, and set up the hanging of the court gate. So Moses finished the work.¦layout ªlast_verse!…¤book§chapter(«first_verse"ªlast_verse&¦verses•„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙcThen a cloud covered the tent of the congregation, and the glory of the LORD filled the tabernacle.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ”And Moses was not able to enter into the tent of the congregation, because the cloud abode thereon, and the glory of the LORD filled the tabernacle.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsAnd when the cloud was taken up from over the tabernacle, the children of Israel went onward in all their journeys:¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^but if the cloud were not taken up, then they journeyed not till the day that it was taken up.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFor the cloud of the LORD was upon the tabernacle by day, and fire was on it by night, in the sight of all the house of Israel, throughout all their journeys.¦layout ªlast_verse&